\title{A tuple taken apart in a loop body no longer leaks}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-16}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{compiler}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1045}
\import{base-macros}

\p{A reference-counted value taken out of a tuple inside a \code{\verb~|while~} body, including the result of a loop inside a loop, is released at its last use. Before, one count was left in every round. See [prob-NQ7X](prob-NQ7X). \pr{1045}.}
